title: Espalier
text: A fruit tree trained flat against a wall. The trunk feeds the branches one after another, never two at once, and whatever a branch does to the sap, the next branch inherits.
trick: a twister is not reversible: a beam sent back along a branch does not retrace, it takes the twister's next arm. So head-on mirrors at the branch tips walk the tree clockwise, each branch fed by the one before; a filter on a branch colours all later ones, and a doppler on the trunk shifts the light both ways, so the lowest right branch gets a colour that is on no other branch
motif: pictogram (espalier tree: trunk and two tiers of branches, open lanes in a wall field)
expect: reversals>=3, recolours>=2
